@tradition department-cup
// The department cup: every fourth Monday (week 4 of the cycle: days 22, 50, 78...), the gym on Deck 3, after running
// club. A rowing relay between departments; Commander Vance keeps the board (he tops the gym's rowing leaderboard).
// Five teams, so the small departments row together: Bridge (command, helm, comms) and Commons (galley, garden, store,
// infirmary). The tally keeps the week's winner for chatter and the board.
k: 456
title: Department cup
when: every 4 weeks monday week 4
at: 20:15-21:15
min: 25
where: 3 pool gym
who: vance always, gym-regular 80%, runner 65%, everyone 20%
host: vance
from: vance
ties: tally cup choices=works|watch|survey|bridge|commons mode=teams
ties: decor cupBoard
invite: host=vance odds=25% line="Department cup in the gym tonight. Works is a rower short."

== mail
- The department cup is tomorrow, {time} in the gym: a rowing relay, one team for each department. I keep the board. The board does not lie.

== ask
- Department cup tonight. Come and cheer for your lot.
- Rowing relay tonight. My arms already hurt, and we haven't started.   #funny
- Vance has polished the cup again. It's a mug on a stand.   #funny

== here
- Pull! Pull! Pull!
- Change over, quick!
- The board does not lie.   #funny

== thanks
- You cheer your department through the relay. Vance chalks every time on the board, very neatly.

== chatter
- The department cup is just a mug. We'd still fight for it.   #funny
- Vance timed my row to a tenth of a second. I didn't ask him to.   #funny
- Whoever wins the cup won't stop talking about it for a month.   #funny
